Here are some reasons that I've not yet seen posted:

1)  NetHack has a nearly supernatural ability to heartily SCREW you
    just when you think that you've got it licked. ;)

2)  Rivalry on the system scoreboard can be great fun,

3)  Winning your first game of NetHack... well, it's like winning a
    game of Bubble Bobble, for those of you who are vid freaks enough
    to catch my analogy.  It's like a pathetic but real sort of 
    ACCOMPLISHMENT, especially considering all those times that you
    die due to (1) before you ever win. ;)

4)  For myself, I think that my prime attraction to NetHack is simply
    that you never really get a chance to relax for real -- even when you
    think you've covered every loophole, every way that the game could
    possibly deny you, there's always something that you're not remembering,
    or that you haven't seen yet...  or that you're too tired to remember.
    <grin>




